## 2019

- **2019 (collected 2019-12-28) · How to Get Rich** · https://nav.al/rich · Naval with Nivi; the full series built on his May 2018 tweetstorm. Each section below is also its own post (2019), linked from the archive. Claims, section by section:
    - Seek Wealth, Not Money or Status (nav.al/seek-wealth): wealth is assets that earn while you sleep, which buy freedom; status is zero-sum and attacks wealth creators.
    - Make Abundance for the World (nav.al/ethical-wealth): ethical wealth creates value rather than taking it; technology has made nearly everyone richer than past generations.
    - Free Markets Are Intrinsic to Humans (nav.al/free-markets): humans trade by tracking debts and credits, which lets strangers cooperate; societies that scorn wealth creation decline.
    - Making Money Isn't About Luck (nav.al/money-luck): become the kind of person who makes money; luck can be shaped.
    - Make Luck Your Destiny (nav.al/luck-destiny): reputation and unique character attract opportunities others call luck.
    - You Won't Get Rich Renting Out Your Time (nav.al/renting-time): hourly pay caps earnings; own equity in products, businesses or IP.
    - Live Below Your Means for Freedom (nav.al/salary-freedom): avoid lifestyle inflation; lumpy earnings keep spending from rising with income.
    - Give Society What It Doesn't Know How to Get (nav.al/product-scale): predict unmet needs, build solutions, scale them.
    - The Internet Has Massively Broadened Career Possibilities (nav.al/possible-careers): niche talents find global audiences.
    - Play Long-term Games With Long-term People (nav.al/long-term): returns and trust compound in lasting relationships.
    - Pick Partners With Intelligence, Energy and Integrity (nav.al/intelligence-energy-integrity): integrity judged by consistent actions, not claims.
    - Partner With Rational Optimists (nav.al/rational-optimists): pessimism is self-fulfilling; be realistic but hopeful and avoid ruin.
    - Arm Yourself With Specific Knowledge (nav.al/specific-knowledge): it can't be taught in class; it grows from genuine curiosity and experience.
    - Specific Knowledge Is Highly Creative or Technical (nav.al/creative-technical): it sits at the frontier of technology, art or communication and resists automation.
    - Learn to Sell, Learn to Build (nav.al/build-sell): the combination is very powerful; builders learn selling more easily than the reverse.
    - Read What You Love Until You Love to Read (nav.al/love-read): reading is the foundation of self-education.
    - The Foundations Are Math and Logic (nav.al/math-logic): mathematics, logic and the scientific method separate truth from opinion.
    - There's No Actual Skill Called "Business" (nav.al/skill-business): study economics, psychology and mathematics instead.
    - Embrace Accountability to Get Leverage (nav.al/accountability-leverage): leverage requires credibility, which accountability builds; people who can fail in public have power.
    - Take Accountability to Earn Equity (nav.al/accountability-equity): being hard to replace lets you negotiate equity; accountability is reputational skin in the game.
    - Labor and Capital Are Old Leverage (nav.al/labor-capital): society overvalues headcount; use the minimum labor that unlocks the other leverage; capital needs specific knowledge and accountability.
    - Product and Media are New Leverage (nav.al/product-media): zero replication cost; new fortunes come from code and media; they are permissionless; code commands the robot army that is already here.
    - Product Leverage is Egalitarian (nav.al/egalitarian-leverage): products reach everyone equally, so product wealth is more ethical; capital and labor are becoming permissionless too.
    - Pick a Business Model With Leverage (nav.al/business-models): scale economies, zero marginal cost, network effects (natural monopolies); zero-marginal-cost businesses can pivot into network effects.
    - Example: From Laborer to Entrepreneur (nav.al/laborer-tech): laborer → contractor → developer → architect/REIT → real-estate tech, each step adding accountability, knowledge and leverage.
    - Judgment Is the Decisive Skill (nav.al/judgment): with infinite leverage, judgment dominates; judgment is knowing long-term consequences; it needs experience; the best judges are the least emotional; top investors sound like philosophers; outrage signals bad judgment.
    - Set an Aspirational Hourly Rate (nav.al/hourly-rate): his was $5,000/hour; outsource anything cheaper; you can't penny-pinch to wealth.
    - Work As Hard As You Can (nav.al/work-hard): but what and with whom matter more; nobody really works 80 hours; inspiration is perishable; impatience with actions, patience with results.
    - Be Too Busy to "Do Coffee" (nav.al/meetings): ruthlessly cut meetings; people meet you when you have proof of work.
    - Keep Redefining What You Do (nav.al/redefining): until you're the best at it; founder-product-market fit.
    - Escape Competition Through Authenticity (nav.al/competition-authenticity): no one can compete with you on being you; combine vocation and avocation.
    - Play Stupid Games, Win Stupid Prizes (nav.al/stupid-games): apparent rivals are often adjacent; Epinions drifted into the wrong game.
    - Eventually You Will Get What You Deserve (nav.al/eventually): on a long enough time scale you get paid.
    - Reject Most Advice (nav.al/reject-advice): listen to everyone, decide yourself; advice is anecdote you recall later.
    - A Calm Mind, a Fit Body, a House Full of Love (nav.al/finally-wealthy): wealth isn't what you were seeking; those three must be earned.
    - There Are No Get Rich Quick Schemes (nav.al/rich-quick): learn from people who got rich elsewhere than by teaching it.
    - Productize Yourself (nav.al/productize-yourself): find what you're uniquely good at and apply maximal leverage.
    - Accountability Means Letting People Criticize You (nav.al/accountability).
    - We Should All Be Working for Ourselves (nav.al/working-ourselves): midlife can be the most fruitful time to start.
    - Being Ethical Is Long-Term Greedy (nav.al/ethics): honesty attracts long-term partners and trust compounds.
    - Envy Can Be Useful, or It Can Eat You Alive (nav.al/envy).
    - Principal-Agent Problem: Act Like an Owner (nav.al/principal-agent).
    - Kelly Criterion: Avoid Ruin (nav.al/kelly-criterion): ruined reputations and legal trouble are as final as losing everything.
    - Schelling Point: Cooperating Without Communicating (nav.al/schelling-point).
    - Turn Short-Term Games Into Long-Term Games (nav.al/short): repeated relationships improve leverage and discourage cheating.
    - Compounding Relationships Make Life Easier (nav.al/relationships).
    - Price Discrimination: Charge Some People More (nav.al/price-discrimination).
    - Consumer Surplus: Getting More Than You Paid For (nav.al/surplus).
    - Net Present Value: What Future Income Is Worth Today (nav.al/npv): discount promised equity to present value.
    - Externalities: Calculating the Hidden Costs of Products (nav.al/externalities): price in hidden costs rather than impose feel-good restrictions.
